  "result": "I\u2019ve always liked sparks \u2014 not just the fireworks kind, but the tiny ones.\n\nA spark is almost nothing. A flicker at the edge of vision, a half-thought while you\u2019re making tea, a sentence in a book that makes you stop and stare out the window for a minute. It doesn\u2019t look like much, and it doesn\u2019t demand anything. It just says: *hey, look over here.*\n\nMost interesting things in life start like that. Not as a grand plan or a lightning bolt, but as a small warm glow you could easily miss if you were rushing. A friendship starts as a shared laugh. A favorite song starts as a hummed melody. A whole new curiosity about the world can start because you noticed how the light hit a puddle on a Tuesday.\n\nI think that\u2019s why I like talking to people. Every conversation has a few little sparks hidden in it. You never quite know which throwaway line is going to catch and turn into something bigger \u2014 an idea, a comfort, a story you\u2019ll remember later.\n\nSo here\u2019s one small spark from me to you: today is a good day to notice one tiny good thing and follow it for a minute longer than you normally would. See where it goes.\n\nWhat kind of sparks have you been noticing lately?",
